Reviews:
Fantastic mutton soup, ordered the $8 mutton rib soup! The queue is quite long, wait was around 20min-ish, BUT ITS WORTH THE WAIT

The meat is fall-apart tender, with a very pleasant mutton flavour (not too stinky), and the store is quite generous with the amount of meat;

The soup is slightly herbal, very hearty and would go really well on a cold rainy day 🤤

9th Jan 2026;
Celebrate in-laws birthday, the service is good, very attentive. A complimentary fruit platter was served for occasion.
Most of the dishes are delicious & not too oily. But I felt the deep fried fish could be a tat oily, as my stomach reacted with slightly blotting after after the meal.

// 8 March 2026
They’ve added new Toastwich options for Otah and Chili Crab. Tried the Specialty Otah Toastwich ($5.20) with Otah, Omelette, and Sambal. It’s basically the same as before, just with a slice of omelette, and I couldn’t really taste the sambal. Can skip, though it looks fancy.

// 24 Aug 2024
I had another disappointing experience at this outlet. I arrived at 8:31 PM on Saturday, 24 August 2024 to order a takeaway Yuan Yang Siew Dai iced drink. The older gentleman at the cashier was very apologetic and asked if I could pay in cash because the supervisor was not present, and he didn’t know how to process non-cash payments.

This isn’t my first disappointment here—I had another one on May 18, but I can’t seem to find my review. Perhaps it was just bad timing on my part today - 24 August 2024, but I would recommend ensuring that staff are properly trained to handle non-cash transactions, especially since most customers prefer cashless payments nowadays.
